        "biography": "Jacqueline Durran\u00a0(born January 1966) is a British\u00a0costume designer. She has received numerous accolades, including two\u00a0Academy Awards, three\u00a0British Academy Film Awards, a\u00a0British Academy Television Craft Award, and two\u00a0Costume Designers Guild Awards.\n\nDurran is best known for her collaborations with directors\u00a0Mike Leigh,\u00a0Joe Wright, and\u00a0Greta Gerwig. She has received nine nominations for the\u00a0Academy Award for Best Costume Design and has won twice for\u00a0Anna Karenina\u00a0(2012) and\u00a0Little Women\u00a0(2019). She has also been nominated for the\u00a0BAFTA Award for Best Costume Design\u00a011 times, with three wins for\u00a0Vera Drake\u00a0(2004),\u00a0Anna Karenina, and\u00a0Little Women.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Jacqueline Durran, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.",
